<urn:atm:triage:finding/RSH-004>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "RSH-004" ;
  triage:title "Sha256Digest::of(&str) is declared infallible, but sc-sha's calculate_hash returns a Resul" ;
  triage:description "Sha256Digest::of(&str) is declared infallible, but sc-sha's calculate_hash returns a Result (D0, line 145-146 says ShaError::InvalidUtf8 'cannot occur'). The plan does not say what 'of' does on an Err. Panicking on the send path (record before every Transport::send) would violate M-PANIC-ON-BUG for a non-bug. Separately, sc-sha normalizes CR and CRLF to LF, so for any text that is not compact serde_json the digest is not SHA-256 of the bytes. The plan covers the committed queries as LF-only. The query text hashed at extract.rs:231 is input.query, which can be user-supplied and contain CRLF. Its query_sha256 would then no longer match the bytes it claims to identify. Recommendation: Say that 'of' handles the unreachable Err arm without panicking. For example, treat it as a documented unreachable with a deterministic fallback, or keep 'of' returning Result at the one send-site call. Note that query_sha256 identifies LF-normalized query text, and keep the 'digest equals SHA-256 of the sent bytes' claim to request bodies only. This is a wording and behaviour clarification, not a new gate." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-a-refine" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "RSH" ;
  triage:severity "minor" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-11-07T22:47:54Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:A1-PLAN67 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-11-07T23:55:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
